Answer: A nested loop is a loop written inside another loop.

```java
for (int j = 1; j <= 3; j++) {
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
System.out.println("Hello");
}
}
```

The inner loop represents a task that is repeated by the outer loop.

Answer: In:

```java
for (int j = 1; j <= 3; j++) {
for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
System.out.println("Hello");
}
}
```

The loop using j is the outer loop. The loop using i is the inner loop. The inner loop completes its repetitions for each iteration of the outer loop.

